course: dictionary
lesson: 12498
title: Departed: leaving, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Departed is the past form of depart, which means to leave, especially to start a journey. «The train departed at 9:15.» Use the clues: a time and a journey tell you the train left the station at 9:15.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The train left at 9:15» still makes sense, so left is a good meaning for departed here.
explain: Departed can also be used more gently. «We remembered our dear departed grandmother» means she has died. Writers use this softer word to talk about sad news. «The team departed from their usual plan» means they changed away from the usual way.
fact: Depart means to leave, especially to start a journey.
fact: Departed is the past form of depart: depart, departs, departed, departing.
fact: «Departed» can mean someone has died. It is a gentle, polite way to say it.
fact: «The departed» means people who have died.
fact: «Departed from» means changed away from the usual way, as in «departed from tradition».
exercise: «The train departed at 9:15.» What does departed mean here? | *Left a place to start a journey | Broke down on the track | Stayed behind at home | Arrived at a station
exercise: «The bus departed at 10:20 and arrived at 11:05.» How long was the journey? | 25 minutes | 35 minutes | 1 hour 45 minutes | *45 minutes
exercise: Dad says, «We remembered our dear departed grandmother.» What does departed mean? | Someone who has gone on holiday | Someone who is very tired | Someone who is very late | *Someone who has died
test: «The team departed from their usual plan and tried something new.» What does departed from mean here? | Ran faster than before | Stayed exactly the same | *Changed away from the usual way | Left the field to go home
test: Which word is the past form of depart? | *Departed | Departure | Departs | Departing
exam: Which meaning does departed have in «the dear departed»? | *People who have died | Lost in the crowd | Changed from the usual way | Left on a journey
